#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:98 index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: primary
#: index.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "introduction"
msgstr "introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword;, is a full featured <acronym>WYSIWYG</acronym> (What You See Is What "
"You Get) Word-processor/Desktop Publishing Program."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "&koffice;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "applications"
msgstr "aplicacions"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; is part of the &koffice; productivity suite for the K Desktop "
"Environment. Other applications in &koffice; include:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kspread; (A spreadsheet application.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpresenter; (A presentation creator.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "&karbon14; (A vector drawing program.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kivio; (A flowchart creator)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krita; (A pixel based drawing program.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kexi; (An integrated environment for databases.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kchart; (A chart and graph creator.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<application>KPlato</application> (An integrated project management and "
"planning tool.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "and a simple integrated office desktop, to help organize your work."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All &koffice; applications were designed from the beginning to take "
"advantage of the features of &kde;. Because of this, &kword; (like all of "
"&koffice;), supports many advanced features you expect from todays desktop "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; is a word-processor which can work either as a traditional word "
"processor, or as a simple but powerful desktop publishing application. This "
"is possible because &kword; is a frame oriented word processor, not a page "
"oriented word processor (&Microsoft; <application>Word</application>,"
"&Wordperfect; and <application>Applixware</application> are all page "
"oriented word processors)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Frame oriented word processors work by creating one or more "
"<emphasis>frames</emphasis> per page. Each frame acts as a boundary (like a "
"frame which surrounds a photograph), which limits the text to the boundaries "
"of the frame. You can move and re-size boundaries to define exactly where on "
"the page the text will be placed. As you re-size frames, the text is "
"reworked to fit within these frames."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:157 index.docbook:169 index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid "Button"
msgstr "Boton"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can easily <emphasis>connect</emphasis> one frame to the next. When you "
"connect two frames, any text which does not fit within the first frame, "
"flows easily and automatically into the next."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In addition to text, you can include virtually anything inside a frame. A "
"frame can contain a spreadsheet, pictures, a database form, or nearly any "
"piece of data. Since each page can have any number of frames, documents can "
"appear quite sophisticated while still remaining easy to edit."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; users also benefit from the auto wrap features of &kword;. When you "
"place one frame on top of part of another frame, the text from the "
"<emphasis>lowest</emphasis> frame can be automatically wrapped around the "
"newly created frame. This reformatting occurs in a <acronym>WYSIWYG</"
"acronym> Graphical User Interface, and happens automatically while you edit."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: index.docbook:196 index.docbook:783 index.docbook:801 index.docbook:851
#: index.docbook:898 index.docbook:1358
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: index.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid "features"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As a word-processor, &kword; includes the most used options of many other "
"word processors, while maintaining a simple interface. In addition to the "
"features you expect from a modern word-processing package (text entry, bold "
"face, italics, text alignment, text printing, &etc;), &kword; can:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use predefined templates, to generate complex document layout with one click "
"of the mouse. As a user, you can build your own templates, download "
"templates from the web, or use the current document to create a new template."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; provides automatic numbering of lists and automatic bulleting of "
"lists with any character or shape you want."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Define paragraph layout styles, frame layout styles and table layout styles, "
"to shorten the editing time of your document, and ensure consistency "
"throughout a long document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Edit headers and footers for your documents. You can have different headers "
"for even and odd pages, or the same headers throughout."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Search through your document for text. You can further refine your search by "
"specifying font, format, font size and many other features of the text. By "
"adding wild-cards to your search, the search and replace functions can "
"become very powerful."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Footnotes and Endnotes. &kword; has all the tools necessary to manage "
"footnotes or endnotes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tables. You can either use the table formatting capabilities of &kword;, or "
"you can import any spreadsheet from &kspread;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; has built in support for KParts. KParts allows you to insert any "
"spreadsheet, picture, chart, graph, document, or any other data type from "
"any &koffice; application. You are free to edit that KPart using the tools "
"designed for that task, without needing to start the application at all."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; can zoom in or out to make the editing of your documents easier on "
"any computer, and with any font size."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; supports customizable toolbars and menus."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; has extensive internationalization support including right-to-left "
"and left-to-right text flow."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can embed formulas directly into &kword; using the integrated formula "
"editor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can have &kword; auto-correct many of the most common spelling and "
"punctuation mistakes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; can check the spelling of your document. &kword; can automatically "
"mark misspelled words as you type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can access an on-line thesaurus (English only) to find the exact word "
"you are looking for."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; can automatically create a table of contents, and keep it up to date."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; has optional autocompletion for commonly used words."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; has support for document bookmarks, to easily navigate large "
"documents.."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; has support for Internet hyperlinks and email addresses."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; has the ability for proofreaders to make comments about portions of "
"the text. These comments are stored in the &kword; file, and can be changed "
"or deleted easily."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:285
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; can merge data from an outside database, spreadsheet, document or "
"text file to create mailinglists, form letters, invoices, etc."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; can load and save documents from other wordprocessing programs with "
"an extensive list of filters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; can create PDF files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can edit one document from multiple views. This allows you to have "
"several windows open on <emphasis>one document</emphasis>. Edits in one "
"window are immediately updated in the other window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; can surround your frames with borders and you can set the background "
"color of each frame separately if you want."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:300
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; has several accessibility features, including the ability to speak "
"all or part of a document using Text-to-Speech (KTTS) and manipulate "
"documents using the keyboard only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The best part about &kword;, is the effort that has been placed to make "
"&kword; a productive tool for all your needs from the simplest letter, to "
"the most complex document you might need to work on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid "What parts of this guide should I read?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: index.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "getting started"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Anyone who has looked at the table of contents has surely come to the "
"conclusion that reading this manual from cover to cover, is an unreasonable "
"(and fortunately unnecessary) task."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This user guide is designed to be helpful to a wide variety of users, from "
"the very experienced, to the novice user. Since different users will have "
"different needs, each section of this manual is self-contained. The user is "
"not expected to have read all of the previous sections of the manual to find "
"the instructions useful."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To help determine what should be read before starting to work with &kword;, "
"a suggested reading list for three levels of users is given below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If each of these sections is read <emphasis>before</emphasis> starting to "
"use &kword;, using &kword; will be easier."
msgstr ""

