msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:479
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced Topics"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:480
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The sections that are included in this chapter are for advanced users. The "
"instructions for these sections will assume you are familiar with the basic "
"operation of &kword;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: chapter
#: index.docbook:481
#, no-c-format
msgid "&struct; &mmerge;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:491
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:492
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next part of &kword; documentation is designed to provide examples on "
"how to solve specific problems using &kword;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:494
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each section is a self contained list of steps, and refers the reader to "
"other sections of the documentation for more complete information on "
"different aspects of &kword;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:496
#, no-c-format
msgid "These examples were selected to:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Show how &kword; might function differently from other word processors you "
"are used to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show how to combine several elements to create the desired document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid "Illustrate the power of &kword;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:502
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use these examples as recipes for your document, or modify them to "
"create the look or content you desire."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:505
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How do I get the pages numbers on the outsides of the pages and the title in "
"the middle of the header (like a novel)?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: index.docbook:507
#, no-c-format
msgid "insert page numbers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:509
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This first example shows how you can combine center tabs and variables in a "
"header to create a common format to your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:510
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Your document must be at least 2 pages long <emphasis>before</emphasis> you "
"begin this procedure."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Document Information</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:514
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the <guilabel>General</guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:515
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click once in the text box labeled <guilabel>Title</guilabel> with the &LMB; "
"and enter the desired document title."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:517
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:518
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Page Layout...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:520
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the <guilabel>Header &amp; Footer</guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:521
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select <guilabel>Different header for even and odd pages</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:522 index.docbook:539 index.docbook:557
#, no-c-format
msgid "Then click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:523
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Enable Document "
"Headers</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:525
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Move to an odd numbered page in your document, and click in the header box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:526
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Paragraph...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:528 index.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Paragraph Settings</guilabel> dialog will appear. Click on the "
"<guilabel>Tabulators</guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:529 index.docbook:553
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click the <guibutton>New</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:530 index.docbook:554
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the arrows of the spinbox labeled <guilabel>Position</guilabel> enter "
"a value that is exactly 1/2 the frame width. The frame width is listed "
"directly below the <guilabel>Position</guilabel> spin box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:532 index.docbook:556
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the <guibutton>Center</guibutton> radio button in the section entitled "
"<guilabel>Alignment</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:534
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click the <guibutton>New</guibutton> button again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:535
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the arrows of the spinbox labeled <guilabel>Position</guilabel> enter "
"a value that is slightly less than the frame width. The frame width is "
"listed directly below the <guilabel>Position</guilabel> spin box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:537
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the <guibutton>Right</guibutton> radio button in the section entitled "
"<guilabel>Alignment</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:540 index.docbook:558
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click in the header again with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:541 index.docbook:562
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Type the &Tab; key. This will move the cursor to the center of the header."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:542 index.docbook:563
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Variable</"
"guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>Document Information</"
"guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Document Title</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the "
"menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:545
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Type the &Tab; key again. This will move the cursor near the right margin of "
"the header."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:546 index.docbook:559
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Variable</"
"guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>Page</guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Page Number</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:549
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Move to an even numbered page in your document, and click in the header box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:550
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Paragraph</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:567
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"That completes the procedure. Your document now has the title of the "
"document in the center along the top of each page, and the page numbers on "
"the outside corners of the pages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:569
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want page numbers on the bottom of the pages, you can use <link "
"linkend=\"headers-and-footers\">Footers</link> instead of headers in your "
"document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:574
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I create a <literal role=\"extension\">.pdf</literal> file?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: index.docbook:575
#, no-c-format
msgid "creating a PDF file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: index.docbook:576
#, no-c-format
msgid "PDF, creating"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:578
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; differs slightly from other word processors here. Instead of saving "
"your file as a <literal role=\"extension\">.pdf</literal> file, you "
"<emphasis>print</emphasis> your file to create the <literal role=\"extension"
"\">.pdf</literal> file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are ready to create a <literal role=\"extension\">.pdf</literal> "
"file from your document:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:584
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Print</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:586
#, no-c-format
msgid "This will bring up the <guilabel>Print</guilabel> dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:587
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the combo box labeled <guilabel>Name</guilabel>, select <guilabel>Print "
"to File (PDF)</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:588
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter your desired filename in the <guilabel>Output file:</guilabel> text "
"box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:589
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you wish to make any changes to the PDF formatting, select "
"<guibutton>Properties</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:590
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A complete explanation to all these properties, is beyond the scope of this "
"document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:591
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr "Clicatz sus <guibutton>Validar</guibutton>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Your PDF file will be created and saved at the location specified in "
"<guilabel>Output file</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:594
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on printing in &kde;, visit <ulink url=\"http://"
"printing.kde.org\">The &kde; Print web page</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:599
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I remove template categories from the startup dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Templates can only be removed using the <guilabel>Create Template</guilabel> "
"dialog. For instructions, click <link linkend=\"template-delete-group"
"\">Removing template group</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:619
#, no-c-format
msgid "Questions and Answers"
msgstr "Questions e responsas"

#. Tag: primary
#: index.docbook:620
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>FAQ</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:625
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When I try to load a document or picture, it does not appear in my dialog "
"box, but I know I saved it there. Why can I not see it?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:629
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check to make sure that you have selected the correct file type in the <link "
"linkend=\"file-dialog\">open dialog box</link>. If you save a file in one "
"format, but ask &kword; to show you the files from another format, you will "
"not see your saved file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:637
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"What is a <literal role=\"extension\">kwd</literal> file? What is a <literal "
"role=\"extension\">kwt</literal> file?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:641
#, no-c-format
msgid "A <literal role=\"extension\">kwd</literal> file is a &kword; document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:642
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <literal role=\"extension\">kwt</literal> file is a &kword; template file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:648
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where can I get updates?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:651
#, no-c-format
msgid "For updates to &kword; you should always check the following sites:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:652
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &koffice; website (<ulink url=\"http://koffice.kde.org\">http://koffice."
"kde.org</ulink>) is the first place to look for updates. Any software "
"updates, bug fixes or announcements of new releases of &koffice; will be "
"found here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:654
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Addons for &koffice; can be found at <ulink url=\"http://koffice.kde.org/"
"addons/\">http://koffice.kde.org/addons/</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:660
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do themes affect &kword;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:663
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; (like all of &koffice;) is completely themeable. You can use any QT "
"or &kde; theme to customize the look of &kword;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:669
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I use &kword; to read &Microsoft; Word files?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:672
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; does have the ability to import &Microsoft; Word files. The "
"conversion process is not perfect, and some formatting information will be "
"lost. For more details please refer to the <link linkend=\"filters\">Import/"
"Export Filters</link> section of the documentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:680
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I save my &kword; document as a &Microsoft; Word file?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:683
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the moment, &kword; does not yet provide support for exporting to "
"&Microsoft; Word documents. If you need to exchange documents with MS Word, "
"you should use Rich Text Format as an intermediate file format. Rich Text "
"Format files are converted well by both &Microsoft; Word and &kword;,"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:693
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I save my &kword; document as a PDF file?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:696
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. Instructions on creating a PDF file are found <link linkend=\"qd-pdf"
"\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:703
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I have to exchange documents with a friend who does not have &kword;; what "
"is the best way to do this ?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:707
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"What you and your friend need to do is agree on a file format that both word "
"processors can read and write effectively. Rich Text Format is probably a "
"good choice."
msgstr ""

