#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:901
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction to Filters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:902
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; has the ability (with varying success) to load data from foreign "
"(non-&koffice;) data files. &kword; also has the ability to save data as non-"
"&koffice; data files. This is provided to help users of &kword; to interact "
"more seamlessly with people who use other operating systems and "
"wordprocessors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:908
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; does this by loading a non-&koffice; datafile into memory and "
"passing the data through a <emphasis>filter</emphasis> to extract as much "
"information as possible from the data file. Some formatting information will "
"be lost or changed by the filter in the attempt."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:914
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When &kword; reads data <emphasis>into</emphasis> &kword; from a non-"
"&koffice; file format, it is <emphasis>importing</emphasis> the data."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:919
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When &kword; saves a &kword; document as a non-&koffice; file format, it is "
"<emphasis>exporting</emphasis> the data."
msgstr ""

