msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: index.docbook:1808
#, no-c-format
msgid "Vector Image"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1810
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A vector based graphic is described in terms of lines and shapes, not in "
"terms of dots. These files scale better than bit-mapped images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: acronym
#: index.docbook:1817
#, no-c-format
msgid "WYSIWYG"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1819
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Stands for <emphasis>What You See Is What You Get</emphasis>. &kword; is a "
"<acronym>WYSIWYG</acronym> word processor, which means that the document "
"will appear the same on the screen while you are editing it, as it will on "
"the printed page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: index.docbook:1827
#, no-c-format
msgid "&X-Window;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1829
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &X-Window; (also known simply as <quote>X</quote>) is required for "
"&koffice; to operate. More information on &X-Window; for &Linux; can be "
"found at <ulink url=\"http://www.xfree86.org\">http://www.xfree86.org</ulink>"
msgstr ""
